BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/exhibition-on-screen-michelangelo-love-and-death/2026-09-27/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T160000
DTSTAMP:20260921T164243Z
CREATED:20260706T154448Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T164243Z
UID:10006918-1790517600-1790524800@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Exhibition on Screen | Michelangelo: Love and Death
DESCRIPTION:Michelangelo – Love and Death offers a cinematic journey through the great chapels and museums of Florence\, Rome and the Vatican\, to the print and drawing rooms of Europe\, to explore Michelangelo’s tempestuous life. The film goes in search of a greater understanding of this charismatic and enigmatic figure\, both through his relationships with his contemporaries and his ongoing artistic legacy. The film invites audiences to intimately examine Michelangelo’s art and artistic process – from the Carrara quarries where Michelangelo sourced his marble\, to the new technology being used to attribute works. The film also offers a rare chance to get up close to the mesmerizing Rothschild Bronzes\, which\, following an extensive research project carried out by Academics in Cambridge in 2015\, were positively attributed to Michelangelo after over a century of debate. \nPurchase Tickets
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/exhibition-on-screen-michelangelo-love-and-death/2026-09-27/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Film
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Untitled-Real-Estate-Flyer-e1782841875569.png
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Asheville Art Museum 2 South Pack Square Asheville NC 28801 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2 South Pack Square:geo:-82.5512827,35.5946714
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Highland Brewing": "https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/killer-whale/", "Where Y'at AVL Music": "https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/killer-whale/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Highlandbrewing": "https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/killer-whale/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:highlandbrewing
X-SOURCE:Highland Brewing, Where Y'at AVL Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T170000
DTSTAMP:20260817T130049Z
CREATED:20260817T130049Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260817T130049Z
UID:10029767-1790517600-1790528400@highlandbrewing.com
SUMMARY:Killer Whale
DESCRIPTION:Bio:\nKiller Whale is a New Orleans-based music project masterminded by singer-songwriter and musician Thomas Johnson. The band’s signature style straddles multiple worlds\, blending the soulful\, rhythmic bounce of Southern R&B with the hazy\, sun-drenched vibe of West Coast surf folk and dream pop. Johnson’s bi-coastal lifestyle between Louisiana and California deeply influences this distinctive sound\, often affectionately labeled as “pontoon soul” or “dreamy funk”. \nWeekend Live Music\nHighland Brewing’s weekend live music series showcases incredible local talent\, regional acts and national touring bands from across the East Coast and beyond. Free and open to all ages (unless noted otherwise)\, it’s the perfect excuse to gather your crew\, listen and vibe to a wide range of genres including soul\, bluegrass\, acoustic\, country\, folk and more.\nLive music typically takes place on our scenic Meadow stage. Shows are rain or shine\, if the weather doesn’t cooperate and we have time to move inside\, the band will play in the Taproom where there’s still plenty of room to boogie.\nChairs\, blankets and well-behaved\, leashed pets are welcome in the Meadow. Please note that coolers and outside alcohol are not permitted on the premises.
URL:https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/killer-whale/
LOCATION:Meadow at Highland Brewing Co.\, 12 Old Charlotte Highway\, Suite 200\, Asheville\, NC\, 28803\, United States
CATEGORIES:Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://highlandbrewing.com/wp-content/uploads/Untitled-design176.png
END:VEVENT
