X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Hendo Fun Friends": "https://www.meetup.com/https-www-meetup-com-hendo-fun-friends/events/316559357/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_hendo_fun_friends
X-SOURCE:Hendo Fun Friends
UID:event_316559357@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045050Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T092000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T150000
SUMMARY:Max Patch Bald\; a Saunter
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nHike a section of the famous Appalachian Tr
 ail on top of Max Patch Mountain. This 4\,600-foot mountain was cleared an
 d used as pasture in the 1800s. Today\, it's a 350-acre tract of open land
  on a high knob with 360-degree views. On a clear day\, you can see from M
 t. Mitchell on the east to the Great Smoky Mountains on the south.\nBefore
  we get there\, we will take a side stop at Little Falls Branch Falls\nWe 
 are the Sloth Hike Team of WNC: “We will get there when we get there.”
  We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike groups don’t !! This event is d
 ependent on ‘nice’ weather.\n**John Muir didn’t like the word ‘hik
 e’. *“We ought to saunter through them reverently\, not 'hike' through
  them.”***\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI curre
 ntly have 4 driver(s) (=16ppl)\n(the group will be split into 2 groups - q
 uicker & slower.)\n**WE WILL SPEND (up to) an HOUR AT THE ‘TOP’ TO ‘
 ENJOY’.** Bring ground cloth\, snacks & water.\n**MAX PATCH** details::\
 nDifficulty: Well developed easy trail\; constant gradual climb.\nLength: 
 2.0 mi total\; Total ascent: 275 ft\; Pace: **1.5mph**\nBefore we get ther
 e\, we will take a side stop at:\n**LITTLE FALLS BRANCH FALLS** details:\n
 Length: 0.5 mile\; one-way\; Ascent: 100 ft\nDifficulty: woodland trail\; 
 w/ 2 rockhop creek Xings\n**Total Drive Time:** 1.25 hr/60 mi (one way) We
  will be driving I-40 west to the Harmon Den exit (7)\; then 6 miles on a 
 steadily climbing gravel forest rd. (hi-clearance suggested)\n**Google Map
 s: “Max Patch Parking”**\n**Return Not earlier than: 3:00 pm**\n**Carp
 ool contributions appreciated. $10.00 suggested**\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICI
 PANT HIKE.** This event is NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the an
 tics of fun-loving dogs. Dogs (and Masters) required to be ‘on-leash'. S
 mall (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will drive themselves.\nWeather Che
 ck: Del Rio\, TN\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an affa
 ir.\nWe suggest open windows while carpooling. Only you know your own heal
 th status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health or the
  health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing 
 your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nAll hikes 
 are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate
  equipment.\nWaiver: There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activ
 ity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to rel
 ease from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Aff
 iliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal lo
 ss which might occur while participating in this activity or while traveli
 ng in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agrees to a
 bide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructio
 ns of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from the g
 roup.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected on th
 is trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: Cur
 mudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(on day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\n**Pi
 cs: [https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums](https://www.flick
 r.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums)**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/https-www-meetup-com-hendo-fun-friend
 s/events/316559357/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260914T210310Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T210310Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
