X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Avl Digital Nomads": "https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/315656930/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_avl_digital_nomads
X-SOURCE:AVL Digital Nomads
UID:event_315656930@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045037Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T193000
SUMMARY:AVL Digital Nomads - Book Club
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n**October 2026 Selection - *Drive Your Plo
 w Over the Bones of the Dead* by Olga Tokarczuk**\n[Amazon](https://www.am
 azon.com/Drive-Your-Plow-Over-Bones/dp/0525541330/) - [GoodReads](https://
 www.goodreads.com/book/show/51648276-drive-your-plow-over-the-bones-of-the
 -dead)\n\n*In a remote Polish village\, Janina devotes the dark winter day
 s to studying astrology\, translating the poetry of William Blake\, and ta
 king care of the summer homes of wealthy Warsaw residents. Her reputation 
 as a crank and a recluse is amplified by her not-so-secret preference for 
 the company of animals over humans. Then a neighbor\, Big Foot\, turns up 
 dead. Soon other bodies are discovered\, in increasingly strange circumsta
 nces. As suspicions mount\, Janina inserts herself into the investigation\
 , certain that she knows whodunit. If only anyone would pay her mind . . .
 *\n\n*A deeply satisfying thriller cum fairy tale\, Drive Your Plow over t
 he Bones of the Dead is a provocative exploration of the murky borderland 
 between sanity and madness\, justice and tradition\, autonomy and fate. Wh
 om do we deem sane? it asks. Who is worthy of a voice?*\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\
 n**Welcome to our monthly Book Club!** We’re a small\, friendly group th
 at gets together for fun\, thoughtful conversations about a different book
  each month.\n\nFinished the whole book? Great. Only made it through a few
  chapters? Still come. Didn’t read it at all but the discussion sounds i
 nteresting? Honestly\, you’re welcome too.\nWe meet on the **first Tuesd
 ay of every month**.\n\nOne of the best things about this group is that we
  keep it relatively small and guide the conversation\, so it doesn’t tur
 n into three people talking while everyone else quietly questions their li
 fe choices. Everyone has a chance to jump in\, share their thoughts\, and 
 explore the book’s characters\, themes\, writing\, and bigger ideas.\n\n
 You definitely don’t need to be a literary expert. Whether you read cons
 tantly or you’re trying to get back into it\, this is a relaxed place to
  discover new books\, hear different perspectives\, and meet some great pe
 ople along the way.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/315656930/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260712T185335Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260712T185335Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Shutupandwriteasheville": "https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/316587274/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_shutupandwriteasheville
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_316587274@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045107Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T193000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write!® - Downtown
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\n***\\*\\*\\*Please 
 note: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this M
 eetup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\n**Here's how it works
 .** Show up at or before 6:00. At 6:00\, we do some quick introductions. A
 fterward\, for a full 60 minutes (I'll set a timer!) we are heads-down wri
 ting. Writing what? A novel? You bet. Some poetry? Sure. Song lyrics? Your
  resume? That report you need to get to your boss before 8 AM or you'll *n
 eed* *to write* that resume? All of the above and more. Just shut up and w
 rite.\n\nSurrounding ourselves with other writers who are busy putting wor
 ds onto page (physical or virtual) keeps us all accountable and focused.\n
 \nWhen the timer goes off\, we'll check-in with each other and see how it 
 went. Afterward\, feel free to stay to chat and get to know your fellow wr
 iters\, or keep writing\, or take off.\n\nSocializing is optional and will
  happen after (or briefly before) the focused writing. This is a safe spac
 e to work on your craft. No one will read or critique your writing.\n\nFor
  more information about our events\, visit [https://shutupwrite.com](https
 ://shutupwrite.com).\n\n**What to Expect**\n\n* Roughly 15 minutes of intr
 oductions\n* 60 minutes of focused writing (somebody set a timer)!\n* Afte
 rward\, optional socializing\n\n**Being late is okay:** Just show up and g
 et settled\, then check in with the host after the session. (Look for the 
 person with the Shut Up & Write sign).\n\n**What Should I Bring?**\n\n* Wh
 atever you need to be able to write!\n* Earbuds/earplugs if you want to bl
 ock ambient noise.\n\n**Other Important Details:**\n\n***\\*\\*\\*Please n
 ote: Shut Up & Write event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! web
 site and this Meetup page will be closed. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\nHOSTS: This is a mult
 i-host event\, so most of the time there will be a host present. If we are
  unlucky and no host can attend\, please find each other and self-organize
 . Pay attention to the event chat and comments to see who is available.\n\
 nWI-FI: Yes!\n\nPARKING: Street parking in metered spots is free after 6pm
 . Closest municipal garages ($2/hour) are Wall St. & Coxe Street/Sears All
 ey.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/316587
 274/
