SUMMARY:Community Day | The Art of Paper
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Art Museum invites you to visit for free on Saturday\, October 10 between 11am–5pm! Come celebrate the exhibition The Art of Paper with an afternoon of creativity and community engagement—featuring live music\, art activities\, exhibition tours\, and more. \nSCHEDULE OF EVENTS\n11am–5pm: Free admission to the Museum\, including the featured exhibition\, The Art of Paper.  \n11:30am–3:30pm: Live piano in the Windgate Foundation Atrium with Willie Sime.  \nNoon\, 1pm\, and 2pm: The Art of Paper 30-minute Express Tours.  \n12:30pm\, 1:30pm\, and 2:30pm: Warp\, Weft\, and the Grid\, 30-minute Express Tours. \n2–2:15pm\, 3:15–3:30pm: Asheville School student dance performance in Explore Asheville Exhibition Hall (level 3)\, featuring Warp\, Weft\, and the Grid.  \n2:30–3pm: Asheville School student dance and poetry performances in The Art of Paper. \nPreregister—let us know you’re coming! \n  \nThis Community Day is generously sponsored by:
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/community-day-the-art-of-paper/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Community Event
