DTSTAMP:20260926T045106Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T140000
SUMMARY:The French Broad Chocolate Factory & Cafe ~ Factory Tour & Chocola
 te Tasting
DESCRIPTION:Senior Singles Fun Bunch\n**The French Broad Chocolate Factory
  Tour consists of a classroom session which will cover the history of the 
 factory\, overview of the cacao farming\, and some yummy chocolate tasting
  where we will taste four different types of chocolate! 😋 Then we will 
 go on a guided tour of the chocolate factory where we will see the chocola
 te process making thru large viewing windows.**\n\n**TOURS:** **The tours 
 last 45-55 minutes. Please arrive 10-15 minutes early to check in at the c
 afe counter.**\n\n**COST:** **Adults ~ $12 plus tax = $14.23 total (no sen
 ior discount 😞)**\n\n**BOOK YOUR RESERVATION:** **You must book your re
 servation online for the tours are popular and limited in space. If you pl
 an on going please book now!! Be sure you book the** **BEAN TO BAR CHOCOLA
 TE FACTORY TOUR for October 16\, Friday at 1:00 PM.** **After you book the
 n RSVP here on this meetup**\n**event.** **Book your reservation on websit
 e below. ⬇️ By the way\, it was a bit confusing for me to find the tou
 r to book (it may be for you\, too) just look at the top of the page for t
 ours. If you still can’t get it please call me or call the factory direc
 t and have them book you. Good luck!**\n\n**WEBSITE:** **www.frenchbroadch
 ocolates.com**\n\n**GIFTSHOP & STORE:** **In case you want to buy chocolat
 e for your friends & family ~ or extras for yourself!**\n\n**CAFE:** **Aft
 er the tour we can stop in the factory cafe for even more chocolate (Yes!)
 \, baked goods\, bonbons\, ice cream\, coffee or wine. ☕️ 🍷 Menu is
  online at the above website.**\n\n**PARKING: 🅿️** **Parking is free 
 and on-site right next to the building. How convenient! There is handicapp
 ed parking available and a ramp up to the factory building.**\n\n**PETS:**
  **🐶** **Sorry ~ no pets allowed except certified service animals.**\n\
 n**I hope you will come join me. I’ve been wanting to do this tour for a
  long time. So come and let’s indulge in some chocolate together!! 😋*
 *\n\n**QUESTIONS/CONCERNS:**\n**Shae.kemerer@aol.com**\n**(828)699-8180 (T
 ext or call)**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/seniorsinglesfunbunch/events/31609351
 6/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260813T005007Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260813T005007Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/history-and-archaeology-of-the-arboretum/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T160000
DTSTAMP:20260908T154259Z
CREATED:20260801T084646Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260908T154259Z
UID:1778780019701-1792155600-1792166400@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:History and Archaeology of the Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:History and Archaeology of the Arboretum\nwith Bob and Mary Noel \nFriday\, October 16  |  1 – 4pm \nRegister Here!\n  \nThe land that makes up The North Carolina Arboretum has been home to different human groups over a span of more than 15\,000 years. It has had many uses and been shaped by those who lived here. This walk\, led by archaeologists Bob and Mary Noel\, will give participants a chance to see and hear about past occupants of this land\, and even a little history about how it became the state’s Arboretum. \nBob and Mary Noel both had long careers as archaeologists with the US Forest Service. Bob worked mostly in North Carolina where he recorded thousands of sites on national forest lands here. Most of Mary’s archaeological work was in Idaho and Ohio. Both of them have been active in living history programs as well\, most recently with the Heritage Alliance in Jonesborough\, Tennessee. The Noels now have a consulting firm and still do archaeological survey projects. Mary can be found working at the Arboretum’s Baker Information desk several days a week\, sharing her knowledge of local trails\, gardens and history. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/history-and-archaeology-of-the-arboretum/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/BentCreek_logging-.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/fall-tree-id-october-26/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T160000
DTSTAMP:20260904T193123Z
CREATED:20260904T193123Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T193123Z
UID:1778780019781-1792155600-1792166400@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Fall Tree ID
DESCRIPTION:Fall Tree ID\nWith Lauren Lampley \nFriday\, October 16  |  1pm – 4pm \nBRN – Core  |  BREG – Elective \nRegister Here!\nJoin this class as we discuss how to use different characteristics and field guides to identify common trees of Western North Carolina found here at the NC Arboretum. We will look at using different characteristics including habitat\, bark\, buds\, growth pattern\, leaf shape\, and fruit/nut shape to identify trees. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nLauren Lampley began her career at Grandfather Mountain Stewardship Foundation as a Park Naturalist which solidified Lauren’s interests in ecology and a passion for teaching others. She has led walks and hikes in a variety of subjects from Geology to Birding and especially enjoys learning and teaching about our local ecology. She currently works at the NC Arboretum as the Adult Education Coordinator managing all the programming hosted through the Adult Education Department. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/fall-tree-id-october-26/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BREG,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/GreatTrees-Sourwood.jpg
END:VEVENT
