SUMMARY:Fire Ritual
DESCRIPTION:Senseful Soul’s Asheville Healing Community🧘🏻‍♀️
 🏳️‍🌈🪐🔮\nGather round the fire and we hold space for this a
 ncient elemental practice of protection and cleansing.\nFire has long been
  associated with healing and protection\, its flames believed to possess t
 he power to cleanse\, ward off evil\, and bring about transformation.\n\nT
 his evening we will gather around our own sacred fire. In ancient times fi
 re was not just a practical necessity but a spiritual force that connected
  the people to the divine.\nThats what we are cultivating this evening.\n\
 n**Together we will:**\nHonor the element of fire\nSet energetic protectio
 ns\nLead you through a guided meditation\nConnect with plant spirits for s
 acred release\nDiscuss the importance of this time of year\nAnd more\n\n**
 About your guides**\n***Jenn (She/Her)*** is an intuitive healer trained Y
 oga Teacher 9+ years\, Reiki Master\, Astrologer and Spiritual Coach. She 
 combines her knowledge of the body from 13 years working in physical thera
 py with all spiritual tools that have contributed to her own healing & spi
 ritual journey to help guide others.\n***Vi (They/Them)*** is a practicing
  Witch & Psychic who is a trained Yoga Teacher\, Reiki Master\, and Tarot 
 Reader. They combine their passions of astrology\, divination\, dance\, an
 d creative expression to help others listen to their intuition.\n***Alessa
 ndra Mary (she/her)*** is a ceremonialist\, Akashic priestess\, mystic\, a
 uthor\, and sacred storyteller devoted to the path of remembrance. Through
  sacred gatherings and oracular transmissions\, she weaves soulful experie
 nces that invite you into deeper connection with synchronicity\, authentic
 ity\, and the unseen magic woven through everyday life. She stewards the l
 and we will be gathering on.\n\n**Donation suggestion:** $25-$35\n\n**PLEA
 SE NOTE:** Pre-registration is required for this event to honor the capaci
 ty of the space. If you would like to skip the fees\, you can Venmo us you
 r donation [here](https://venmo.com/u/iamalessandramary "https://venmo.com
 /u/iamalessandramary")
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/senseful-soul-s-asheville-healing-com
 munity-%EF%B8%8F-%EF%B8%8F/events/316669529/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260922T211408Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T211408Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Cuddle Collective": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-cuddle-collective/events/316674085/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_cuddle_collective
X-SOURCE:Asheville Cuddle Collective
UID:event_316674085@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045030Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261023T185000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261023T230000
SUMMARY:Oct 23rd Queer Platonic Cuddles 
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\n**[REGISTER HERE](https://www.zef
 fy.com/en-US/ticketing/oct-23rd-queer-platonic-cuddle)**[ ](https://www.ze
 ffy.com/en-US/ticketing/oct-23rd-queer-platonic-cuddle)(rsvp's on Meetup d
 o not count as registering)\nThis is an event for Adults who identify as L
 GBTQIA+.\nThe intention of this event is to build community and provide a 
 supportive place for participants to explore sweet platonic physical touch
 .\nNo one turned away for lack of funds (please ask if you truly need a sc
 holarship or work trade).\n**This is a sweet & welcoming event where we pr
 actice and use verbal consent to connect and share touch.** We talk about 
 boundaries and practice both saying and receiving a “no”. In this spac
 e it is common to see people cuddle\, share massage\, have their hair brus
 hed\, laugh\, cry\, and be vulnerable. This is a sober space where we can 
 relax and connect with other humans who are seeking touch based connection
 .\nWe strive for this to be a safe event. Safe touch enhances our ability 
 to connect with and trust people. When we are in a space of safety\, we ar
 e able to relax\, feel comfort\, and be vulnerable.\n\nConsent and respect
  are at the forefront of the experience. We strive for a safe and welcomin
 g environment\, fostering a sense of trust that allows attendees to fully 
 enjoy shared touch without any pressure or expectations.\n\nDiscover the j
 oy of shared vulnerability in an environment where your authenticity is no
 t just accepted but celebrated. This event is an opportunity to connect wi
 th like-minded individuals who appreciate the simplicity of human touch an
 d the profound impact it can have on our well-being.\n\nExpress yourself i
 n a way that feels true to you\, whether through cozy attire or a touch of
  personal flair. We encourage individuality and self-expression\, creating
  an inclusive space where everyone can be their authentic selves. Dress co
 de is Casual and cozy.\n\nThis is an inclusive environment where we will a
 im to foster the dismantling of and no tolerance of ableism\, fat-shaming\
 , homophobia/transphobia\, sexism\, xenophobia\, classism\, racism & other
  ideas that lead to folks feeling disconnected or unwelcome.\n\n**THE RULE
 S**\n1\\. Pants stay on for the whole event\\.\n2\\. You do not have to to
 uch anyone at this event\\.\n3\\. You must ask permission and receive a ve
 rbal YES before you touch anyone\\. Please be specific in your requests\\.
 \n4\\. If you feel a yes\\\, say YES\\. If you feel a no\\\, say NO\\. If 
 you’re a maybe\\\, say NO\\. You can always change your mind\\.\n5\\. Ge
 t your facilitator if you have a question or concern\\\, or if you need as
 sistance with anything during the event\\.\n6\\. Talking\\\, laughter\\\, 
 silence\\\, silliness\\\, stillness\\\, and crying are welcome\\.\n\n**ETI
 QUETTE**\n\n* ARRIVE ON TIME: It is important that all participants arrive
  before the Welcome Circle.\n* Please be free of strong scents\; many folk
 s would rather not be close to someone who smells of perfume\, essential o
 ils\, or cigarettes\n* BE SOBER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at
  this event.\n\n**WHAT TO BRING:** personal water bottle and snacks to sha
 re. The only thing that you are required to bring is a clean and sober you
 .\n\nWe take individual and group safety seriously! if you experience\, se
 e\, or know that one of our participants is not safe to be at a touch base
 d event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our best to cr
 eate a safe environment which means that if someone is causing harm (physi
 cal or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes harm that ta
 kes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and know that 
 some of our participants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\n\\*r
 efund policy- Full refund if you cancel 7 days before the event or you can
 cel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to covid. Credit towar
 ds a future event if you cancel more than 3 days before an event. No refun
 d if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-show.
