SUMMARY:Oct 30th An Evening of Spicy/Sensual Snuggles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. use the link below to reserve
  your ticket-\n**[https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/oct-30th-an-evenin
 g-of-sensual-snuggles](https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/oct-30th-an-e
 vening-of-sensual-snuggles)**\n\nWhat is a Sensual Snuggle Event?\\*\\*\nT
 his is a sweet & welcoming event where we practice and use verbal consent 
 to connect and share touch. We talk about boundaries and practice both say
 ing and receiving a “no”. In this space it is common to see people cud
 dle\, share massage\, have their hair brushed\, kiss\, expose nipples\, pl
 ay\, laugh\, cry\, and be vulnerable. This is a sober space where we can r
 elax and connect with other humans who are seeking touch based connection.
 \nWe strive for this to be a safe event. Safe touch enhances our ability t
 o connect with and trust people. When we are in a space of safety\, we are
  able to relax\, feel comfort\, and be vulnerable.\n\n**Our Agreements:**\
 n1- We ask for what we want an wait for a yes before touching others.\n2- 
 We say no if we don’t want to do something.\n3- We try to receive a no w
 ith grace and not take it personally.\n4- We arrive on time\, clean (as sc
 ent free as possible)\, and sober.\n5- We keep our pants/shorts on at this
  event. (Tops are optional\; this is a sensual space\, not a sexual space.
 )\n6- We are here to connect with others. Connection can be verbal\, plato
 nic\, or spicy!\n7- We welcome diversity. Isms and Phobias are not welcome
  here!\n\n**Who should attend:**\nPeople who are interested in safely expl
 oring touch and sensuality with strangers. This includes people who are si
 ngle\, people who are not single\, couples\, folks who are new to town and
  looking for connection\, people of all/any genders and sexual orientation
 s\, people of all ages (18 and up). People who understand and respect cons
 ent\, who will take care of themselves and people around them. This event 
 is queer-normative. The guest list will include all genders\, orientations
 \, ages\, and personalities. If that’s not your thing… This is not the
  event for you.\n***Who should NOT attend:***\n-People who are only lookin
 g for a sex party.\n-People who do not understand and respect consent.\n-P
 eople who have extreme fear of setting and speaking their personal boundar
 ies\; in order to create a safe space we need to know that you will say 
 “no” if you feel a no.\n-People who are homophobic\, racist\, sexist\,
  ageist\, ableist…\n-People under 18 years of age.\n***Schedule of the E
 vening***\n\n\\*6:50pm Doors Open\, Mix & Mingle\n\n* 7:00pm We gather in 
 a circle to meet each other\, build a container\, cover consent and bounda
 ry setting and discuss event agreements. Then we will play a few intimacy 
 building games to meet and connect with other people in the room. Please m
 ake sure you arrive on-time!\n\\*8:15pm Once the container is built we wil
 l have self directed snuggling and sensual interactions until the end of t
 he party.\n* 10:50pm Closing Circle\; a time to re-center and connect as a
  group to verbally share anything that came up at the event or to voice gr
 atitude to someone(s) you enjoyed interacting with.\n\\*11:00pm cleanup & 
 head home\; you are welcome to help.\n\n**We take individual and group saf
 ety seriously!** If you experience\, see\, or know that one of our partici
 pants is not safe to be at this event we want to know about it. We are com
 mitted to doing our best to create a safe environment which means that if 
 someone is causing harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome he
 re (this includes harm that takes place outside of our events). We stand b
 ehind survivors and know that some of our participants are here to heal fr
 om touch based trauma.\n\nThese events are not "gender balanced"[. Check o
 ut our website for more information about this decision.](http://holdmeavl
 .com/why-i-dont-gender-balance-events/)\n\n**Simple definitions/clarificat
 ions-** Platonic- marked by the absence of romance or sex.\nMost of the in
 teractions we have with friends and strangers are platonic.\nSensual- grat
 ification of the senses or the indulgence of appetite.\nWe might feel sens
 ual when we feel someone's breath on our neck or experience a extra long a
 nd slow caress.\nSexual- having or involving sex.\nOften involving one mor
 e more peoples genitals\; perhaps seeking orgasm.\n\\*Refund Policy- Full 
 refund if you cancel 7 days before the event or you cancel due to illness\
 , emergency\, or direct exposure to covid. Credit towards a future event i
 f you cancel more than 3 days before an event. No refund if you cancel wit
 hin 2 days of the event or no-show.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-cuddle-collective/events/31
 6674224/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260923T033423Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923T033423Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
