X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_avl_digital_nomads
X-SOURCE:AVL Digital Nomads
UID:event_315657080@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045037Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T193000
SUMMARY:AVL Digital Nomads - Book Club
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n**December 2026 Selection - *When Breach B
 ecomes Air* by Paul Kalanithi**\n[Amazon](https://www.amazon.com/When-Brea
 th-Becomes-Paul-Kalanithi/dp/081298840X/) - [GoodReads](https://www.goodre
 ads.com/book/show/25899336-when-breath-becomes-)\n\n*At the age of thirty-
 six\, on the verge of completing a decade’s worth of training as a neuro
 surgeon\, Paul Kalanithi was diagnosed with stage IV lung cancer. One day 
 he was a doctor treating the dying\, and the next he was a patient struggl
 ing to live. And just like that\, the future he and his wife had imagined 
 evaporated. When Breath Becomes Air chronicles Kalanithi’s transformatio
 n from a naïve medical student “possessed\,” as he wrote\, “by the 
 question of what\, given that all organisms die\, makes a virtuous and mea
 ningful life” into a neurosurgeon at Stanford working in the brain\, the
  most critical place for human identity\, and finally into a patient and n
 ew father confronting his own mortality.*\n\n*What makes life worth living
  in the face of death? What do you do when the future\, no longer a ladder
  toward your goals in life\, flattens out into a perpetual present? What d
 oes it mean to have a child\, to nurture a new life as another fades away?
  These are some of the questions Kalanithi wrestles with in this profoundl
 y moving\, exquisitely observed memoir.*\n\n*Paul Kalanithi died in March 
 2015\, while working on this book\, yet his words live on as a guide and a
  gift to us all. “I began to realize that coming face to face with my ow
 n mortality\, in a sense\, had changed nothing and everything\,” he wrot
 e. “Seven words from Samuel Beckett began to repeat in my head: ‘I can
 ’t go on. I’ll go on.’” When Breath Becomes Air is an unforgettabl
 e\, life-affirming reflection on the challenge of facing death and on the 
 relationship between doctor and patient\, from a brilliant writer who beca
 me both.*\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n**Welcome to our monthly Book Club!** We’re
  a small\, friendly group that gets together for fun\, thoughtful conversa
 tions about a different book each month.\n\nFinished the whole book? Great
 . Only made it through a few chapters? Still come. Didn’t read it at all
  but the discussion sounds interesting? Honestly\, you’re welcome too.\n
 We meet on the **first Tuesday of every month**.\n\nOne of the best things
  about this group is that we keep it relatively small and guide the conver
 sation\, so it doesn’t turn into three people talking while everyone els
 e quietly questions their life choices. Everyone has a chance to jump in\,
  share their thoughts\, and explore the book’s characters\, themes\, wri
 ting\, and bigger ideas.\n\nYou definitely don’t need to be a literary e
 xpert. Whether you read constantly or you’re trying to get back into it\
 , this is a relaxed place to discover new books\, hear different perspecti
 ves\, and meet some great people along the way.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/315657080/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260712T190922Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260712T190922Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
